@participant8 Thanks for the update. I am confirming that after upgrading to 1.0.0 and using your solution, I can query from private S3 buckets. I am doing the following:

```
import duckdb
con = duckdb.connect()
con.query(
    f"""
    INSTALL httpfs;
    LOAD httpfs;
    CREATE OR REPLACE TEMPORARY SECRET secret (
        TYPE S3,
        PROVIDER CREDENTIAL_CHAIN
    );
    """
)

df = con.query("SELECT * FROM read_parquet('s3://my-bucket/test.parquet');")
```

Thanks!

@participant3: can you give it a try using the syntax:
```
INSTALL httpfs; 
LOAD httpfs;
CREATE SECRET secret1 (
        TYPE S3,
        ENDPOINT '***',
        KEY_ID '****',
        SECRET '****',
        REGION '****'
);
```
Wrapping that to Python, and using the relevant credentials?

I believe the problem is that `load_aws_credentials` is now deprecated, see https://duckdb.org/docs/extensions/aws#legacy-features for more details

